  ('cs_adele_career', 'ent_adele', 'career', 'Career', 'Adele Laurie Blue Adkins ( ə-DEL; born 5 May 1988), known mononymously as Adele, is an English singer and songwriter. Regarded as a British cultural icon, she is known for her mezzo-soprano vocals and sentimental songwriting. Her accolades include 16 Grammy Awards, 12 Brit Awards (including three for British Album of the Year), an Academy Award, a Primetime Emmy Award, and a Golden Globe Award.
