  ('cs_charles-strite_career', 'ent_charles-strite', 'career', 'Career', 'Charles Perkins Strite (February 27, 1878 – October 18, 1956) was an American inventor known for inventing the pop-up toaster. He received U.S. patent #1,394,450 on October 18, 1921, for the pop-up bread toaster. Strite then formed the Waters Genter Company and made the pop-up toaster publicly available in 1926.',
